# target — an identifier that resolves to nothing ends the command, rather than
# becoming a plan or an empty answer.
#
# The surface is derived by internal/surfaceaudit.TargetSurface: a command
# entrypoint is a site when it writes its first byte of output before the
# identifier it was handed has had a chance to fail it. Sites are keyed by the
# entrypoint function. See dev/surfaces/README.md for the format.
#
# `cc show` used to sit here as an exemption whose stated reason was that the
# analysis could not see its resolution — the check was on a loop variable
# rather than on a call result. Finding #18 (`cc logs` answered an unknown
# component name with an empty listing at exit 0 while `cc show` refused it)
# was fixed by giving the two commands one resolver, findCustomComponent, and
# the exemption went with it: what an analysis cannot see is usually a shape
# worth changing rather than a rule worth exempting.
#
# The ceiling is the number of sites known to be unproven. It may fall without
# ceremony and may only rise by editing this line on purpose.
#ceiling 0

internal/cmd/dash.go:runDashGrep = exempt: the argument is a search string, not an identifier; "not referenced as a whole value in any dashboard" (with the ent ls --pattern routing, D-10) is the correct answer for a value that appears nowhere
#
# `internal/cmd/ref.go:runRefScan` left this surface in WP7 and its line is gone
# rather than exempted: the target is still a search value with nothing to
# resolve to, but the command now REFUSES one the matcher cannot honour (a
# target that does not start and end on a word character — `ref scan .` matched
# the dot inside every id and returned 2747 hits) before it writes anything, so
# the extractor no longer counts it as printing ahead of its argument's first
# chance to fail. `dash grep` stays: its whole-value match has no such
# precondition, which is why the machinery test anchors on it.

internal/cmd/cache.go:runCacheRefresh = exempt: the category is an enum, not an identifier; an unrecognised value is now refused before any work, so there is no target left to resolve
